      "text": "53-year-old male presenting with cough and breathlessness for 2 weeks. Character: wheezing, worse at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by dust and cold air; relieved by inhaler. Severity 5/10. Associated: chest tightness, sneezing. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 13 years; Hypertension for 4 years; Asthma since childhood. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg; Salbutamol inhaler 100 mcg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: asthma. Personal: smokes bidi daily. Triage: ROUTINE."
